Here is the commit message:
net: Handle unregister properly when netdev namespace change
 fails.

If rtnl_newlink() fails on it's call to dev_change_net_namespace(), we
have to make use of the ->dellink() method, if present, just like we
do when rtnl_configure_link() fails.

Fixes: 317f4810e45e ("rtnl: allow to create device with IFLA_LINK_NETNSID set")
Signed-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>

Here is the root cause:
The bug occurs when the function `rtnl_newlink()` fails during the device namespace change (`dev_change_net_namespace()`) after a successful configuration of the network device. In such cases, the device is not properly unregistered, leading to potential resource leaks or inconsistent states in the network subsystem. The original code did not handle this failure scenario correctly, as it only unregistered the device if the configuration failed, neglecting the need to unregister when the namespace change fails.

